.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt NQSELFTEST 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqselftest
.Nd known answers for every algorithm family
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fn nqselftest void
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqselftest
runs fixed inputs through the public functions of every algorithm
family and compares what they produce with answers built into the
library, the kind of self-test a cryptographic module runs before it is
used (FIPS 140-3, which takes its requirements from ISO/IEC 19790:2012,
section 7.10):
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
SHA-224 to SHA-512/256, SHA3-224 to SHA3-512, SHAKE128 and SHAKE256 of
.Dq abc ;
.It
KangarooTwelve and its 256-bit form of
.Dq abc ,
and of 9,000 bytes with the customization string
.Ql noqtis
(a tree of two chunks);
.It
HMAC-SHA-256 and HMAC-SHA-512 (RFC 4231, test case 2);
.It
ML-KEM-512, -768 and -1024: a key pair and an encapsulation from fixed
seeds, and the decapsulation;
.It
ML-DSA-44, -65 and -87: a key pair from a fixed seed, the deterministic
signature of a fixed message and its verification;
.It
SLH-DSA-SHA2-128f and SLH-DSA-SHAKE-128f: a key pair from a fixed seed;
.It
HQC-128: a key pair, an encapsulation and the decapsulation;
.It
Ed25519 and ML-DSA-44+Ed25519: a key pair, a deterministic signature and
its verification.
.El
.Pp
Each family's keys, ciphertexts, signatures, secrets and return codes
are hashed with SHA-256; a decapsulation or verification that disagrees
changes the hash.
The masked decapsulations and signers run as in normal use.
It takes about a tenth of a second and allocates nothing: its buffers
are one static block of about 44 KB, wiped after each test, so it must
not run in two threads at once.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv NQOK
when every answer matches;
.Dv NQEKAT
when one does not.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
if (nqselftest() != NQOK) {
  fputs("noqtis: self-test failed, not used\en", stderr);
  exit(1);
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-selftest 1 ,
.Xr nqerr 3
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%T FIPS 140-3: Security Requirements for Cryptographic Modules
.%Q NIST
.%D March 22, 2019
.Re
.Rs
.%A M. Nystrom
.%T Identifiers and Test Vectors for HMAC-SHA-224, HMAC-SHA-256, HMAC-SHA-384, and HMAC-SHA-512
.%R RFC 4231
.%D December 2005
.Re
